from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(3,'evs','living-in-harmony','Living in Harmony',
 ('Shambhu and the mango tree','Shambhu and his father sit in the shade of a huge mango tree in a forest. Birds, squirrels and monkeys live in it. Shambhu sees a monkey eat a mango and throw away the seed, and his father says a new plant can grow from that seed. That is how animals and plants help each other, and how we all live in harmony.'),
 [('Sharing our home',['We bring some animals and plants into our homes on purpose, and some come on their own, like birds, insects and lizards. Sometimes we do not like them, but we should not hurt them.','We take care of some animals and plants by giving them water, food and shelter.','Animals generally do not hurt us unless they feel threatened, so we should not tease or hurt them, even if we are scared of them.','Elders can tell us which animals and plants they kept at home when they were young.']),
  ('What we get from plants and animals',['Plants give us fruits, vegetables, shade, fresh air, wood for houses, fibre for clothes, medicines and shelter for animals.','Cows, buffaloes and goats give us milk and loving company. We respect these animals and treat them with kindness and care.','We depend on plants and animals for food, shelter, clothing and companionship, and they also depend on us for care and protection.']),
  ('How animals and plants help each other',['Animals help plants by dispersing their seeds. A monkey eats a mango and drops the seed, and a new plant grows from it. Dispersing means spreading seeds far and wide.','Animals also make the soil fertile through their waste. Fertile soil is rich in what plants need, so plants grow well and spread.','Plants give animals food and shelter in return. This gives balance, which means each one gets what it needs and nobody loses.','Thousands of trees are planted by squirrels by accident. They bury nuts and forget where they hid them, and some of the nuts sprout.']),
  ('Getting to know an animal and a plant friend',['We can watch an animal such as a dog, cat, crow or pigeon. We note when and where we first saw it, how it moves, what sound it makes and what it eats.','We can keep a bowl of water and some grains for birds.','When we place sweet, fried and cooked food on the floor, ants come to the food they like. Watching them teaches us how clever and busy ants are.','We can visit a plant friend and talk about how we feel. Looking after a plant helps us to be kind and gentle with all living things.'])],
 [('How does a monkey help a mango tree?',[('The monkey eats a mango and drops the seed.','Animals eat fruits.'),('The seed may fall on soil far from the tree.','This is called dispersing.'),('A new mango plant can grow there.','So the tree spreads.')]),
  ('A cat comes into your house uninvited. What should you do?',[('Do not hurt it, even if you are scared.','Animals attack only when they feel threatened.'),('Keep your food covered and keep the space clean.','This reduces the reason for them to come.'),('Leave it gently or ask an elder to help.','Kindness keeps everyone safe.')])],
 ('Explain how animals and plants help each other and us.',['Animals spread seeds','Animal waste makes soil fertile','Plants give food and shelter','We care for both'],['Animals do not help plants','Plants only give shade']),
 ['We share our homes and surroundings with plants and animals.','Plants give us food, fresh air, wood, medicine and fibre.','Animals spread seeds and make soil fertile.','We should be kind to animals and not hurt them.','Living in harmony means giving and getting from each other.'],
 [M('1',1,'Who saw a monkey eating a mango in the forest?','Shambhu',[('Munni','She is in another story'),('Rishi','He is in another story')],'Shambhu saw the monkey.'),
  M('2',1,'What happens to the seed the monkey threw away?','A new plant can grow',[('It disappears','Seeds can sprout'),('It becomes a monkey','Seeds become plants')],'A seed can sprout into a plant.'),
  M('3',1,'Which of these do we get from plants?','Fresh air',[('Plastic','Plastic is made by people'),('Metal','Metal is not from plants')],'Plants give fresh air, shade and wood.'),
  M('4',1,'What do cows and goats give us?','Milk',[('Wood','Wood is from trees'),('Cotton','Cotton is from plants')],'They give milk and company.'),
  M('5',2,'What does dispersing seeds mean?','Spreading seeds far and wide',[('Eating seeds','That is eating'),('Burning seeds','That harms seeds')],'Animals carry seeds to new places.'),
  M('6',2,'What does fertile soil mean?','Soil rich in what plants need',[('Dry hard soil','That is poor soil'),('Soil with no plants','Fertile soil helps plants')],'Fertile soil helps plants grow.'),
  F('7',2,'Squirrels sometimes plant trees by accident.',True,'They bury nuts and forget them.'),
  F('8',2,'We should hurt animals that we do not like.',False,'We should not hurt animals.'),
  M('9',2,'Why do animals sometimes bite or scratch?','They feel threatened',[('They are always angry','Animals usually avoid us'),('They are hungry for people','They are not out to hurt us')],'We should be gentle with them.'),
  S('10',2,'Animals and plants depending on each other in a balanced way is called living in?',['harmony','Harmony'],'Living in harmony.'),
  M('11',3,'Which of these is a use of plants?','Wood for houses',[('Making metal','Metal is not from plants'),('Making glass','Glass is not from plants')],'Wood comes from trees.'),
  M('12',3,'How can we look after birds near our home?','Keep water and grains for them',[('Chase them away','That would harm them'),('Catch them','Birds should be free')],'Water and grains help birds.')],
 keep=['harmony','fertile','dispersing'])
